<p>Dear Alex,</p>
<p>Thank you for the call on Friday. As promised, I attach v3 of the Master
Supply Agreement with a revised clause 12:</p>
<p>1. General cap: 150% of the Annual Fees, unchanged from v2.<br>
2. Data breach: we have moved. Kestrel's liability for a data breach will
be unlimited only where the breach is caused by Kestrel's gross negligence
or wilful misconduct. All other data breach claims fall under the general
cap of 150%.<br>
3. Indirect loss: as in v2.</p>
<p>This is as far as we can go. Our purchasing board meets on 4 November
and we would like to present an agreed clause 12. Please confirm by Friday
30 October whether Kestrel can accept v3.</p>
<p>Best regards</p>
<p>Dr Felix Brandt<br>
Legal Counsel<br>
Acme Automotive GmbH | Legal Department<br>
T +49 711 0815 3340<br>
f.brandt@acme-automotive.de</p>
